# <type>(<scope>): <description>
# │       │             │
# │       │             └─> Summary in present tense. Not capitalized. No period at the end.
# │       │
# │       └─> Scope: options|model|interception|diagnostics|analyzers|probe|seeding|report|pins|samples|release|deps|docs|tooling (optional)
# │
# └─> Type: feat, fix, docs, style, refactor, perf, test, build, ci, chore

# Body (optional): Explain *what* and *why* vs. *how*


# Footer (optional): Reference issues, breaking changes
# Examples:
#   Fixes #123
#   BREAKING CHANGE: <description>

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Conventional Commits v1.0.0 - https://conventionalcommits.org
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Types:
#   feat:     A new feature (MINOR version bump)
#   fix:      A bug fix (PATCH version bump)
#   docs:     Documentation only changes
#   style:    Formatting only (no code change)
#   refactor: Code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature
#   perf:     Performance improvement
#   test:     Adding or correcting tests, test models or behavior pins
#   build:    Changes to the build system, Taskfile, MSBuild props or dependencies
#   ci:       Changes to CI configuration files and scripts
#   chore:    Other changes that don't modify src or test files
#
# Scopes:
#   options, model, interception, diagnostics   src/TenantGuard.EntityFrameworkCore
#   analyzers                                   src/TenantGuard.Analyzers
#   probe, seeding, report                      src/TenantGuard.Testing
#   pins                                        tests/integration/TenantGuard.BehaviorPins
#   samples                                     samples/
#   release, deps, docs, tooling                packaging, dependencies, docs, repo setup
#
# Breaking Changes:
#   Add ! after type/scope: feat!: or feat(options)!:
#   Or add footer: BREAKING CHANGE: <description>
#   Rule IDs, messages, option names, exception types and the public API are public
#   contracts, fixed by docs/SPEC.md.
#
# Examples:
#   feat(model): report TGM003 when a tenant filter captures a local
#   fix(interception): compare tenant values with the property's ValueComparer
#   test(pins): pin query filters applying to FindAsync
#   feat(analyzers)!: report TG001 as an error
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
